# The forest spider's body (#328, D101, D102): the `dead` frame of spider.grid, pixel for pixel, in a decor-tier palette (D76):
# a dim colour with a contour in its own hue, no ink 0b0814, no moon rim, so a harmless body never reads as a live spider.
# Forest recolour (#236, D108, 2026-11-20): hand-set tone roles (contour k, belly a, abdomen b/c, head h/H, fang f, legs l/L/n)
# on one dark umber (OKLab L 0.164 to 0.253, chroma 0.055, hue 50): a dried husk. Its spots are forest-1's near-black ground and
# the blue night forest behind the ledges; the warm hue keeps it off that blue (D108 band 0.08..0.20); no ink, no moon rim.
# Keep it in step with spider.grid.
size 32 16
color k 1e0600
color a 220800
color b 270b00
color c 2d1001
color h 2a0e00
color H 2f1202
color f 341b0c
color l 2a1103
color L 2f1608
color n 270e01
frame body
